Chapter: GopKey

 Scancode source for Option A payloads running on the H1a runtime
 spine. runtime-init installs the IDT and unmasks the keyboard IRQ,
 so scancodes arrive in the kernel key-buffer cell (28680) from our
 own interrupt handler. Polling data port 0x60 directly would race
 that handler for the byte and lose it. gk-take consumes the cell
 read-and-clear: zero means no key is waiting. codex-vm delivers
 window and -keys scancodes through the same IRQ path once the guest
 has programmed the PIC, so cell consumption behaves identically
 under the emulator, under OVMF, and on metal.

Section: Key Cell

  gk-cell : Integer = 28680

  gk-take : Integer -> Integer
  gk-take (dummy) = bit-and (atomic-exchange gk-cell 0) 255
